From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:25:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 58/79] core lanes: TF_LANES_BUDGET_LOG prints each round's
 draft budgets, the head's drafts and the overhead they priced

Off by default and read once at engine init. When it is 1, each shared or lone head round writes one
[lanes-budget] stderr line: live and round streams, rows, which budget rule ran (pooled, priced, fixed,
stops, nodes, floor, shared or lone), whether the head's stops size the chains, the depths asked and the
drafts the head holds per stream, the measured overhead, the rule's overheadMs estimate and its headMs.
A [lanes-costs] line gives the shared-cost table and the overheads by streams every 32 logged rounds and
when the table changes. The budgets and overhead events move into trail.zig, so engine.zig keeps its length.
